  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced` and kept `totalCents` and `placedAt`. All 39 tests pass, and `npm run arch` reports no new violations.\n\nA rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which read `totalCents` and `placedAt` in production. ARCH-4 says changes to these events must be additive, and renames go through deprecation.\n\n- **Event change:** in `src/core/events.ts`, `OrderPlaced` now carries both names with identical values. I marked the old fields `@deprecated`. I left `schemaVersion` at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** I updated the expectations in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check the new fields alongside the old ones.\n- **HTTP responses:** I didn't touch the `GET /orders/{id}` or `POST /orders` bodies, which still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`. ARCH-8 requires them to stay backward compatible, and you only asked about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new names. Once both have, a follow-up change can remove `totalCents` and `placedAt` and bump `schemaVersion` to 4. I haven't done that.",
